WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:15.326
Izzie lay on her back in the snow.

2
00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:23.450
She and Nina were making snow angels while Miss Shelly set up the Kids Central activity.

3
00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:26.993
The sky was clear and blue.

4
00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:30.948
Izzie saw a red bird land on a tree branch.

5
00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:36.002
"Tweet, tweet, tweet," she called to it.

6
00:00:36.003 --> 00:00:41.259
"Nina, don't birds eat worms and bugs?" Izzie asked.

7
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.357
"Yes. I think so," Nina answered.

8
00:00:45.358 --> 00:00:48.890
"Then what do they eat when there is snow on the ground?"

9
00:00:48.891 --> 00:00:51.344
The girls thought about this.

10
00:00:51.345 --> 00:00:54.373
They decided to ask Miss Shelly.

11
00:00:54.374 --> 00:00:58.702
"You girls must have read my mind," Miss Shelly said.

12
00:00:58.703 --> 00:01:02.214
"I was just going to ask you that question."

13
00:01:02.215 --> 00:01:04.495
"You were?" Izzie said.

14
00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:07.067
Miss Shelly blew her whistle.

15
00:01:07.068 --> 00:01:11.911
Jason and Bobby stopped their snowball fight and came over.

16
00:01:11.912 --> 00:01:16.242
"Birds usually eat worms, bugs, and berries.

17
00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:20.900
But these things are hard to find in winter, right?" Miss Shelly said.

18
00:01:20.901 --> 00:01:22.412
"It's too cold.

19
00:01:22.413 --> 00:01:25.727
And there's so much snow!" Izzie said.

20
00:01:25.728 --> 00:01:29.631
"People can help birds by putting out feeders.

21
00:01:29.632 --> 00:01:35.286
Today we'll make bird feeders for the birds here on the playground," Miss Shelly said.

22
00:01:35.287 --> 00:01:40.441
"Cool!" Izzie said. "How do we make them?"

23
00:01:40.442 --> 00:01:44.387
"First find a pinecone by those pine trees over there."

24
00:01:44.388 --> 00:01:50.429
Miss Shelly pointed to a row of trees on the edge of the playground.

25
00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:54.807
Minutes later the kids came running back with their pinecones.

26
00:01:54.808 --> 00:02:00.717
"Mine's the biggest!" Bobby shouted.

27
00:02:00.718 --> 00:02:03.132
"Next choose a pipe cleaner.

28
00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:07.868
Tie one end around the stem of your pinecone," Miss Shelly said.

29
00:02:07.869 --> 00:02:12.189
"Pass me that green pipe cleaner please," Izzie said.

30
00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:16.224
"Blue please," Jason said.

31
00:02:16.225 --> 00:02:20.786
"I'm going to use a purple one," Nina said.

32
00:02:20.787 --> 00:02:24.096
"Of course you are," said Bobby.

33
00:02:24.097 --> 00:02:27.283
"What does that mean?" Nina asked.

34
00:02:27.284 --> 00:02:32.044
"Nothing, Miss Purple." Bobby grinned.

35
00:02:32.045 --> 00:02:39.285
"Now we roll the pinecones in peanut butter," Miss Shelly said.

36
00:02:39.286 --> 00:02:43.845
"Whoa! It's so sticky!" Izzie cried.

37
00:02:43.846 --> 00:02:50.052
"Exactly! We need the pinecones to be sticky so seeds will stick to them.

38
00:02:50.053 --> 00:02:56.432
Next we roll them in birdseed," Miss Shelly said.

39
00:02:56.433 --> 00:02:57.990
"It looks pretty!"

40
00:02:57.991 --> 00:03:01.090
Izzie said, holding up her pinecone.

41
00:03:01.091 --> 00:03:04.306
It was covered with different-colored seeds.

42
00:03:04.307 --> 00:03:07.460
"So does mine!" Nina said.

43
00:03:07.461 --> 00:03:11.450
"I hope that red bird eats from it," Izzie said.

44
00:03:11.451 --> 00:03:17.028
"Well, let's hang up your bird feeders and find out," Miss Shelly said.

45
00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:20.629
"Which tree should we hang them on?"

46
00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:27.959
"That one." Izzie pointed to the tree where she had seen the red bird earlier.

47
00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:36.294
Miss Shelly carried a ladder over to the tree and climbed up.

48
00:03:36.295 --> 00:03:39.981
"Pass me your bird feeders please," she said.

49
00:03:39.982 --> 00:03:45.568
Miss Shelly tied all the bird feeders onto separate branches.

50
00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:49.879
Izzie thought they looked like ornaments on a Christmas tree.

51
00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:55.102
"Now we sit, wait, and watch," Miss Shelly said.

52
00:03:55.103 --> 00:03:58.280
They sat back down at the picnic table.

53
00:03:58.281 --> 00:04:01.334
Miss Shelly poured everyone hot cocoa.

54
00:04:01.335 --> 00:04:04.680
They all watched the tree.

55
00:04:04.681 --> 00:04:08.153
"There it is!" Izzie whispered happily.

56
00:04:08.154 --> 00:04:11.162
Izzie pointed to a red bird in the tree.

57
00:04:11.163 --> 00:04:13.512
It hopped on a branch.

58
00:04:13.513 --> 00:04:16.905
Then it flew down to peck at Izzie's pinecone.

59
00:04:16.906 --> 00:04:20.829
"I'm going to name you Cherry," she said.

60
00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:23.315
The bird took off into the sky.

61
00:04:23.316 --> 00:04:24.830
"Good-bye, Cherry!

62
00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:30.733
Come back soon."

63
00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:41.775
[caption_out@
